 @end example
 
 @anchor{vpp_amf}
+@anchor{vmafx}
+@section vmafx
+
+Calculate VMAF and the other metrics of the VMAFx library between two video
+streams, on the CPU or on a GPU.
+
+The first input is the distorted video (@code{main}), the second the reference
+video (@code{reference}); they are synchronized with the framesync options. The
+filter passes the distorted frames on unchanged.
+
+The backend follows the input frames: software frames are scored on the CPU,
+CUDA frames on CUDA, imported without a copy. Frames the backend cannot read
+where they are stop the graph with an error that names the backend, the
+input, the layout and every extractor that refuses them; no frame passes
+unscored and no score is printed after such an error.
+
+It requires the VMAFx library (libvmafx). After installing it, enable the
+filter with @code{./configure --enable-libvmafx}.
+
+The options are generated from the library's option groups; the names of the
+@code{libvmaf} filter (@code{n_threads}, @code{n_subsample}) are accepted as
+aliases. The main options:
+
+@table @option
+@item model
+A @samp{|} separated list of models, each @samp{version=}, @samp{path=},
+@samp{name=}, @samp{disable_clip}, @samp{enable_transform} and
+@samp{@var{extractor}.@var{option}=@var{value}} items separated by @samp{:}.
+Default: the library's default model.
+
+@item feature
+A @samp{|} separated list of extra extractors, each
+@samp{@var{name}[=@var{key}=@var{value}:...]} or @samp{name=@var{name}:...}.
+
+@item backend
+@samp{auto} (default), @samp{cpu}, @samp{cuda}, @samp{sycl}, @samp{hip} or
+@samp{metal}. A value other than @samp{auto} is strict.
+
+@item device
+The GPU of the backend for software frames: @samp{auto} or an index.
+
+@item import
+@samp{auto} imports hardware frames without a copy; @samp{device} refuses
+software frames; @samp{host} downloads hardware frames first (logged once).
+
+@item threads, n_threads
+Worker threads of the extractors.
+
+@item subsample, n_subsample
+Score every n-th frame.
+
+@item pool
+The pooling methods of the final score and the windows: any of @samp{min},
+@samp{max}, @samp{mean}, @samp{harmonic_mean}, @samp{median}, @samp{perc5},
+@samp{perc10}, @samp{perc20}, joined with @samp{+}. Default: @samp{mean}.
+
+@item n_stats
+Window length in seconds: the statistics of each window, not a running
+total, as a log line, an NDJSON object and frame metadata.
+
+@item n_stats_frames
+Window length in frames, instead of @option{n_stats}.
+
+@item stats_out
+Where window statistics go: @samp{log} (default), @samp{metadata}
+(@samp{lavfi.vmafx.window.@var{model}.@var{pool}} on the next output frame),
+@samp{file} (needs @option{stats_path}).
+
+@item stats_path
+NDJSON file of the window statistics.
+
+@item log_path
+Report file.
+
+@item log_fmt
+Report format: @samp{json} (default), @samp{xml}, @samp{csv} or @samp{sub}.
+JSON and XML carry the provenance record.
+
+@item score_fmt
+printf format of the scores; @samp{%.17g} is lossless.
+
+@item provenance
+@samp{log} prints the provenance record at init, @samp{report} embeds it
+in the report (a sidecar for CSV and SUB). Default: both.
+
+@item metadata
+Attach the per-frame scores as @samp{lavfi.vmafx.@var{model}} frame
+metadata; frames then leave the filter once their scores are final.
+
+@item cpumask, gpumask, tiny_model, tiny_device, tiny_threads, tiny_fp16, perceptual_weight, profile
+As the @code{libvmaf} filter options of the same names.
+@end table
+
+@subsection Examples
+
+@itemize
+@item
+Score a distorted file against its reference with the default model:
+@example
+ffmpeg -i distorted.mp4 -i reference.mp4 -lavfi vmafx=log_path=vmafx.json -f null -
+@end example
+
+@item
+Statistics of every two seconds, written to a file:
+@example
+ffmpeg -i distorted.mp4 -i reference.mp4 -lavfi vmafx=n_stats=2:pool=min+mean:stats_out=log+file:stats_path=windows.ndjson -f null -
+@end example
+
+@item
+Score CUDA frames without a copy:
+@example
+ffmpeg -hwaccel cuda -hwaccel_output_format cuda -i distorted.mp4 -hwaccel cuda -hwaccel_output_format cuda -i reference.mp4 -lavfi vmafx -f null -
+@end example
+@end itemize
+
+@section vmafx_tune
+
+Score a pass with the VMAFx library and recommend a CRF for the next one.
+
+The inputs are those of the @ref{vmafx} filter: the distorted video first,
+the reference second. At the end of the stream the filter logs
+@samp{recommended_crf=@var{crf} (target_vmaf=@var{t}, observed_vmaf=@var{v},
+n_frames=@var{n})}: the observed mean VMAF of the first model mapped to a CRF
+in the configured range, 0.40 CRF per VMAF point around its middle. For a
+per-clip sweep over real encodes use the vmaf-tune tool.
+
+The filter has the following options:
+
+@table @option
+@item model
+Model spec, as the @code{vmafx} filter's; default: the library's default model.
+
+@item feature
+Additional feature extractors, @samp{|} separated.
+
+@item threads, n_threads
+Worker threads of the extractors.
+
+@item backend, device
+As the @code{vmafx} filter's, for software frames.
+
+@item recommend_target_vmaf
+Target VMAF score; default 95.
+
+@item recommend_crf_min, recommend_crf_max
+CRF range considered; default 18 to 51.
+
+@item recommend_passes
+Number of probe passes (advisory; one pass is scored).
+@end table
+
 @section vpp_amf
 
 Scale (resize) and convert colorspace, transfer characteristics or color primaries for the input video, using AMD Advanced Media Framework library for hardware acceleration.
